column50:
The <map> and <area> tags can't be styled. You should either use javascript to replace the src of the image onmouseover of the <area>, or, ideally, switch to a <a> with CSS background-images<p><pre><code>  <div style="background:url(banner.png)">
    <a id="homelink"
       href=""
       style="position:absolute;
              top:10px;
              left:10px;
              height:100px;
              width:100px;"></a>
  </div>
</code></pre>
And the CSS:<p><pre><code>  <style>
  #homelink {background:url(homelink.png)}
  #homelink:hover {background:url(homelink_hover.png)}
  </style>
</code></pre>
Hope that makes sense.<p>PS: as other noted, there are other sites more suited to specific coding questions (e.g. stackoverflow.com, experts-exchange.com, etc)
